 The list of discovered PuppetDB targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.puppetdbSDCheckInterval` command-line flag.
 
+## scaleway_sd_configs
+
+Scaleway SD configuration discovers scrape targets from [Scaleway](https://www.scaleway.com/en/) Instances.
+
+Configuration example:
+
+```yaml
+scrape_configs:
+- job_name: scaleway
+  scaleway_sd_configs:
+
+    # secret_key is the Scaleway API secret key to use for authenticating API requests (mandatory).
+    # See https://www.scaleway.com/en/docs/identity-and-access-management/iam/how-to/create-api-keys/
+  - secret_key: "..."
+
+    # project_id is the id of the Scaleway Project to discover Instances in (mandatory).
+    # See https://www.scaleway.com/en/docs/organizations-and-projects/concepts/#project
+    project_id: "..."
+
+    # zone is the Scaleway zone to discover Instances in.
+    # By default, "fr-par-1" is used.
+    # See https://www.scaleway.com/en/docs/organizations-and-projects/concepts/#zone
+    #
+    # zone: "..."
+
+    # api_url is the Scaleway API server to query.
+    # By default, "https://api.scaleway.com" is used.
+    #
+    # api_url: "..."
+
+    # port is an optional port to scrape metrics from.
+    # By default, port 80 is used.
+    #
+    # port: ...
+
+    # Additional HTTP API client options can be specified here, such as proxy_url.
+    # See https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/sd_configs/#http-api-client-options
+```
+
+Each discovered target has an [`__address__`](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/#how-to-modify-scrape-urls-in-targets) label set
+to `<ip>:<port>`, where `<ip>` is the instance's public IPv4 address if it has one, or its private IPv4 address otherwise, and `<port>` is the port from the `scaleway_sd_configs` (default port is `80`).
+
+The following meta labels are available on discovered targets during [relabeling](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/):
+
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_arch`: the architecture of the Instance, such as `x86_64` or `arm64`.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_id`: the unique ID of the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_name`: the name of the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_organization_id`: the ID of the Organization the Instance belongs to.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_private_ipv4`: the private IPv4 address of the Instance, if set.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_project_id`: the ID of the Project the Instance belongs to.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_public_ipv4`: the public IPv4 address of the Instance, if it has one.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_region`: the region id, such as `fr-par`, derived from the Instance's zone.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_state`: the power state of the Instance, such as `running`, `stopped` or `stopped in place`.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_tags`: comma-separated list of tags assigned to the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_type`: the [commercial type](https://www.scaleway.com/en/docs/instances/reference-content/choosing-instance-type/) of the Instance, such as `DEV1-S`.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_zone`: the [zone](https://www.scaleway.com/en/docs/organizations-and-projects/concepts/#zone) the Instance is located in, such as `fr-par-1`.
+
+The list of discovered Scaleway targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.scalewaySDCheckInterval` command-line flag, default: 30s.
+
 ## static_configs
 
 A static config allows specifying a list of targets and a common label set for them.
